{
  "_comment": "Budgets of proofline's own tests (issue 266, A277), ENFORCED (enforce true): tests/ci/test-durations-ci.mjs exits 1 on a passing leg when a test is over its test_ms or a file over its suite_ms, and prints OVER BUDGET lines. Milliseconds before timeouts_scale (read like timeouts.scale of the control plane: 0.5 to 10, else 1; CI uses 1). kinds: the A275 defaults (unit 2000/30000, integration 10000/120000, e2e 60000/600000), the built-in fallback for a missing number. dirs: a kind per test directory (the most specific path prefix wins). files: one row per sampled test file, GENERATED, do not edit by hand: per file the maximum over the test-durations artifacts of CI (both Node versions, all legs, the twice run, every available run of CI) x 3 for a test, x 2.5 for a suite measured at 20 s or more and x 3 for a smaller suite, rounded up to 500 ms / 5 s / 10 s, never below an absolute floor of 2000 ms per test and 10000 ms per suite. Regenerate after a deliberate change of the suite: gh run download <run id of a green main run> -D samples/<n> -p 'test-durations-*' for every run you have, then node tests/ci/derive-budgets.mjs samples/1 samples/2 ... > tests/ci/test-budgets.json (the script keeps this header, kinds, dirs and enforce). A budget that fails is fixed at the test; raising a number needs a reason in the pull request. legs: reserved. calibration.nominal_ms: the RUNNER-SPEED reference. Before node starts the wrapper times a fixed workload (15 node spawns, 40 sha256 rounds over 1 MiB, 300 file create/stat/unlink in a private folder) and multiplies EVERY budget by clamp(measured / nominal, 1, 5), on top of timeouts_scale, so a degraded runner (one leg ran 4.9 times slower than its twin in run 43714635797) does not fail an unrelated pull request, and a faster runner is never stricter than the table. The nominal is the median of calibration_ms over the reports of CI (derive-budgets.mjs writes it).",
